# About + Stellar Heights — nav & redesign safety

## Typography
- Do **not** use em dashes (`—`) or en dashes (`–`) in visible website copy. Prefer commas, periods, colons, or a spaced hyphen (` - `).

## Shared navbar (match the rest of the site)
- `/about/` and `/stellarheights/` must use the **same** `#site-nav-style` and `#site-nav-script`.
- That nav must **match the main-site React nav** (home/projects/careers): logo `5rem→6rem`, padding `1.5rem→2rem`, white/80 round burger with hover scale, **right drawer** `#0f172a` (not full-screen Cormorant overlay), links `text-xl font-medium`, accent `#D4AF37`.
- When changing the navbar, update **both** pages together. Do not restyle one page only.

## Next.js client runtime is removed on redesigned pages
Home (`index.html`), About, Projects, and Stellar Heights are **static HTML**. All `/_next/static/chunks/*.js` and `__next_f` flight scripts were purged so React cannot remount the old page (that caused “old design until second refresh”).

**Do not:**
- Re-add `<script src="/_next/static/chunks/...js">`, `__next_f`, or Turbopack bootstrap to these pages
- “Fix” broken interactivity by restoring Next hydration — use our `#site-nav-script` / page scripts instead
- Leave new edits depending on React IntersectionObserver; use `#jankal-static-reveal` / `animate-fade-up`

**Keep:** Next **CSS** (`/_next/static/chunks/*.css`) is fine for Tailwind utilities on About/Projects/Home.
- Use `MutationObserver` on `document` / `documentElement` with `subtree:true` for nav (it fights React and triggers a full old-design remount)
- Hide the React nav with CSS while also removing our nav (leaves no logo/hamburger)
- Run broad regex replaces across `<body>` that can delete redesign sections
- Touch `#about-design-guard`, `#about-fade-fallback`, or luxury `<style id="about-*">` blocks when only fixing nav

**Do:**
- Only edit `#site-nav-style` / `#site-nav-script` (and matching static header/menu if present) for nav work
- Keep soft retries (`setTimeout`) for nav mount — not full-document observers
- After any About edit, verify `about-mvp`, `about-founders`, `about-design-guard`, and `next-bootstrap disabled` (or equivalent) are still present
- Prefer injecting/keeping nav **outside** React-owned `main` content
